MacBook8,1 (A1534, Cirrus Logic CS4208, SSID 106b:6400): internal speaker support.

SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only (derived from the Linux kernel file it patches)
Base: Debian linux-source-6.12 6.12.107-1, sound/pci/hda/patch_cirrus.c
      (sha256 40ebd2a0ce0edc69dcb288efc6d117701c17ce8f96bcc1642b8df360d75c4d2a)

- Hide the combo-jack mic pin 0x18 and the speaker pin 0x1d from the generic parser.
  Enabling input/VREF on 0x18 latches the codec clock (vendor coef 0x1f -> 0x400) and silences the speakers.
- Add a 4-channel 44.1 kHz S16_LE "CS4208 Speaker" PCM on digital converter 0x0a -> pin 0x1d whose
  prepare() programs the TDM path the way EFI does for the startup chime.
- Log the codec clock state once after init.
Requires snd_hda_intel probe_only=2 probe_mask=0x101 single_cmd=1 power_save=0 on the CS4208 controller
(no link reset at probe). See docs/audio/HOW_IT_WORKS.md.

--- a/sound/pci/hda/patch_cirrus.c
+++ b/sound/pci/hda/patch_cirrus.c
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@
